      {
        "id": 125818,
        "name": "Foote",
        "username": "Foote",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/{size}/1877_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-01-07T22:01:51.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"fabikw\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/f/ea5d25/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> fabikw:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I just got my preorder box and was looking at some of the new cards. I noticed something weird in my Prime Warden Haka card. The text on the power in my card says:</p>\n<blockquote>POWER: Play a card. If that card has \"Haka\" in the title, select one target to gain the benefit of your discarding.\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote>\nThe text is different from the one I've seen online and the discard part doesn't make much sense. What's up with this?&nbsp;\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>It was altered slightly for printing. Happens during PTing</p>\n<p>It makes sense when you think about it. Haka plays one of his \"Haka\" cards. Draws 2, then discards X cards. He then chooses a target to gain the benefitial effect of that discarding, whether it be damage reduction from Shielding, healing, or damage from Battle</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
